SPEC IMPRECISION worth recording before P1 builds on it. FR1 opens 'The
launcher emits ACTIVITY_SNAPSHOT only, so a client re-renders the whole
activity block on every update.' The launcher emits no activity events at
all: grepping the tree, ActivitySnapshotEvent appears only in convert.go,
which maps a snapshot INTO a history message, and in its test.

The only path an activity event can reach the stream is a host's
GenAIPartConverter returning one, relayed verbatim at processor.go:288.
So FR1 is still buildable and the requirement is unchanged (consecutive
snapshots for one (messageID, activityType) pair become deltas), but the
interception point is the converter relay, not a launcher-owned emitter.
Confirmed by driving a converter that returns two snapshots for the same
surface: both go out in full, re-sending an unchanged 'shared' field,
which is exactly the waste FR1 removes.

Baseline scope decision: the enforced golden deliberately contains NO
activity updates. The activity-repeat stream will change by design when
FR1 lands, so pinning it here would create a golden that has to be edited
to fit the implementation, which is the failure mode this whole practice
exists to avoid.

